package pages

import "github.com/kiff/cloud/web/internal/components"

// TafsTerms renders /tafs/terms: tafs's terms. It is the source of its
// translations at /<lang>/tafs/terms (<lang>_tafs_terms.templ): change it
// first, then them. Every clause restates KIFF's /terms (§3A is tafs),
// /acceptable-use, or /tafs's prices, and adds no commitment of its own;
// KIFF's Terms cover the rest.
templ TafsTerms() {
	@components.LayoutSiteWithMeta("tafs terms", "The terms for tafs, KIFF's app: who provides it, your account, what a taf does and how you control it, acceptable use, fees, liability and ending.", "website", "", "css/prose.css", "css/legal.css") {
		<article class="legal prose">
			<header class="legal-head">
				<p class="legal-badge">tafs · terms</p>
				<h1>tafs Terms</h1>
				<p class="legal-meta"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 14 November 2026.</p>
				<p class="legal-disclaimer">These terms are for tafs, KIFF's app for iPhone, iPad, Android and computers, and the service behind it. tafs is part of KIFF Cloud, and this page restates what <a href="/terms">KIFF's Terms of Service</a> say about it, adding nothing to them. KIFF's Terms apply to anything this page doesn't cover. Questions: <a href="mailto:legal@kiff.dev">legal@kiff.dev</a>.</p>
			</header>
			<section id="provider">
				<h2>1. Who provides tafs</h2>
				<p>tafs is provided by <strong>Kiff Agents OÜ</strong>, a private limited company in Estonia (registry code 17372313), at Tööstuse tn 75-71, Põhja-Tallinna linnaosa, Tallinn 10416, Estonia. By creating an account or otherwise using tafs, you agree to these terms and to KIFF's Terms. If you accept for a company, you confirm you may bind it.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="account">
				<h2>2. Your account</h2>
				<p>You sign in to tafs with a KIFF account. Give accurate information, keep your credentials confidential, and you are responsible for all activity under your account and for every person you let into it. You must be at least 16 years old, or the age of digital consent where you live, whichever is higher.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="what-a-taf-does">
				<h2>3. What a taf does</h2>
				<p>In tafs you hand a job to a taf: an AI agent that works on a schedule with the tools you connect, inside the KIFF Cards you issue for it. Anthropic provides the AI model it uses. Setup, an AI agent in tafs, helps you connect a tool and set up a taf, but connects nothing by itself: you sign in at the tool's own provider, and approve each connection, the tools a taf may use, and its Cards on your device.</p>
				<p>A taf's reports, messages and memory notes are written by an AI model and can be wrong. Check what matters before you rely on it. Anything a taf writes to someone outside your company says that an AI agent wrote it.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="control">
				<h2>4. Your control: the Card and approvals</h2>
				<p>A taf reaches your tools only through KIFF, which checks every call against the taf's Cards before it is sent. A call within a Card you issued is made on your instruction. A call outside a Card is held or refused, as the Card says. A held call is made only after someone your account allows to answer held calls approves it.</p>
				<p>You choose each taf's job and Cards, answer its held calls, and make sure you may use the tools and accounts you connect. You can halt one taf or all of them, pause a taf, revoke any of its Cards, or remove it. From the moment you halt a taf or revoke a Card, KIFF allows no new call by that taf or under that Card. A request already sent to a tool's provider may still complete: we stop new calls, and can't undo what a provider has done. <a href="/terms#tafs">KIFF's Terms, §3A</a> have the details.</p>
				<p>Under the EU AI Act, Kiff Agents OÜ is the provider of tafs and you are its deployer. Use tafs only for the jobs it offers, and not for any use the AI Act prohibits or classes as high-risk, such as decisions about a person's employment, credit or access to essential services.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="acceptable-use">
				<h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
				<p>You, your people and your tafs must follow the <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>. An agent's action is your action. Among other things, you may not use tafs to break the law, act on a system or account you are not authorized to use, connect a tool with a sign-in that is not yours to give, send spam, or get around a Card, a limit or a hold. We may suspend at once on a credible violation.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="fees">
				<h2>6. Fees</h2>
				<p>At the time of this update, Solo is { tafsEN.Cost.money(TafsSoloCents) } a month, VAT included, with { tafsEN.Cost.number(TafsSoloCredits) } credits a month, sold in the app through the App Store or Google Play. Packs of credits, bought in the app, start at { tafsEN.Cost.money(TafsPackCents[TafsSoloCredits]) }; they don't expire. Each run of a taf uses credits for the AI it used. Coach, and setting tafs up, are included within Coach's fair use. Current prices are on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>; tafs is also part of KIFF's Company plan.</p>
				<p>There is no trial. Solo bought in the app is managed and cancelled in your Apple or Google Play subscriptions, under that store's terms for payment, renewal and refunds. A plan runs to the end of the period you paid for. If you are a consumer in the EU, you may withdraw within 14 days of purchase. <a href="/terms#fees">KIFF's Terms, §8</a> have the details.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="liability">
				<h2>7. Liability</h2>
				<p>tafs is provided "as is" and "as available", except for the warranties in KIFF's Terms (§10). To the extent the law allows, neither party is liable for indirect or consequential damages, and each party's total liability is limited as <a href="/terms#liability">KIFF's Terms, §12</a> say. Nothing limits liability that the law doesn't allow to be limited.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="termination">
				<h2>8. Ending</h2>
				<p>You can stop at any time: delete your account in the app, in Account → <em>Delete account</em>. Export your chats first, from Account → Export my chats. We may end your use for a material breach not cured within thirty days of notice, or at once for an Acceptable Use violation. Your rights to leave and take your data with you are in <a href="/terms#term">KIFF's Terms, §9</a>.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="governing-law">
				<h2>9. Changes and governing law</h2>
				<p>We change these terms the way KIFF's Terms say for their own (§16). They are governed by the laws of the Republic of Estonia, and disputes go to Harju County Court in Tallinn. If you are a consumer in another EU member state, the mandatory consumer-protection rules of your home country still apply.</p>
			</section>
			<section id="contact">
				<h2>10. Contact</h2>
				<p>Contractual questions: <a href="mailto:legal@kiff.dev">legal@kiff.dev</a>. Help with the app: <a href="mailto:support@kiff.dev">support@kiff.dev</a>. Privacy: <a href="mailto:privacy@kiff.dev">privacy@kiff.dev</a>, and how tafs handles personal data is in the <a href="/tafs/privacy">tafs Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
			</section>
		</article>
	}
}
